## TESTING

### Guidelines for Unit Tests

#### XUNIT / .NET

* Follow AAA (Arrange–Act–Assert) for clear test structure
* Keep tests isolated — avoid shared state and static dependencies
* Use test doubles (mocks, stubs, fakes) with libraries like Moq or NSubstitute
* Test only one logical unit per test method
* Use Theory + InlineData / MemberData for data-driven tests
* Prefer constructor injection for sharing setup across tests
* Use IClassFixture and ICollectionFixture for controlled, shared test context
* Name test methods clearly using pattern: *MethodName_State_ExpectedResult*
* Assert using FluentAssertions or xUnit’s built-in assertions
* Avoid asserting multiple independent things in one test
* Mock external services and IO — do not call DB, API, or filesystem
* Test exception flows with Assert.Throws / Assert.ThrowsAsync
* Use helper builders / Mother Objects to simplify Arrange phase
* Keep test project separate from production code and mirror folder structure
* Ensure deterministic tests — no DateTime.Now, randomness, or timing dependencies
* Run tests in parallel only when safe; disable parallelization when needed
* Use code coverage tools (coverlet, ReportGenerator) to identify gaps
* Automate test execution via CI and run on every pull request
* Keep tests fast — under a few milliseconds; move slow tests to integration suite
* Use minimal mocking: mock behavior, not implementation details
* Prefer immutability in tested classes to simplify test setup